      "content": "# Killing a Hung Process on Linux\n\n## 1. Find the PID\n\n```bash\n# By name\npgrep -f \"process_name\"\n\n# Interactively (best for browsing)\ntop          # press 'k' to kill a process\nhtop         # press F9 to kill (if installed)\n\n# Detailed listing\nps aux | grep \"process_name\"\n```\n\n## 2. Kill It (escalating force)\n\n```bash\nkill 12345              # SIGTERM (15) \u2013 polite \"please exit\"\nkill -9 12345           # SIGKILL (9)  \u2013 force kill, no cleanup\nkill -STOP 12345        # SIGSTOP (19) \u2013 freeze it (useful for debugging)\n```\n\n## 3. Kill by Name (no PID lookup needed)\n\n```bash\npkill firefox           # SIGTERM to all matching processes\npkill -9 firefox        # SIGKILL to all matching processes\nkillall firefox         # same idea, different tool\n```\n\n## 4. When Even `kill -9` Doesn't Work\n\nA truly stuck process may",
